Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.58,Default,,0,0,800,,{\b1\4c&H0000FF&\fs40}LAUGHING MAN FANSUBS{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.79,0:00:09.29,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I'm a soldier - that means I'm
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.49,0:00:12.69,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Both a defendant and the judge
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.09,0:00:18.09,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I am standing on both ends of the flame
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.77,0:00:22.87,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Rounding curves
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.07,0:00:25.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Overtaking life and death,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.77,0:00:31.67,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I run and fight with false shadows
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.97,0:00:38.27,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,No matter how many threads of\Ndeception are woven together,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.67,0:00:46.17,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,The truth shall illuminate\Nthe face of light
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.17,0:00:49.97,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save your tears for the day
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.27,0:00:53.27,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,When our pain is far behind
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.67,0:00:56.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,On your feet, come with me
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.57,0:00:59.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,We are soldiers stand or die
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.07,0:01:02.97,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save your fears, take your place
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.17,0:01:06.17,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save them for the judgement day
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.47,0:01:09.37,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Fast and free, follow me
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.67,0:01:14.67,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Time to make the sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.87,0:01:20.47,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,We rise or fall
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.31,0:01:48.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,HQ, I have returned from the Peninsula.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.41,0:01:52.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have some interesting information about Kuze.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.21,0:01:56.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Chief and the Major have been summoned\Nby the Prime Minister, so they're not here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.81,0:01:58.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They told me to listen to your report.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.81,0:02:01.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What situation has a higher\Npriority than my investigation?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.31,0:02:05.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, now there's the possibility that\Nthe refugees are planning a mass uprising.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.21,0:02:08.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Damn, that's not good...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.44,0:02:15.47,Sign - Copy,,650,0,600,,{\b1}The Fact of \N Being There{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.99,0:02:21.82,Dialogue,,350,0,450,,{\b1\i1}Refugee \N \NMeasure \N \NEmergency \N \N Conference{\b0\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.41,0:02:19.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Following the uproar over the mass\Nsuicide of the Individual Eleven,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.31,0:02:23.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,there are reports that refugees throughout\NJapan are gathering at Dejima in Nagasaki
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.71,0:02:28.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in response to the rapidly escalating\Nanti-refugee demonstration.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.67,0:02:30.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The media has been recklessly fanning the flames
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.47,0:02:34.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,by saying that it is a prelude to a mass uprising.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.47,0:02:36.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is there any information that can\Nshed some light on this matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.57,0:02:39.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have received reports that\Nthere have been increasing numbers
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.07,0:02:42.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,of people being apprehended\Nfor illegal entry into Dejima,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.87,0:02:46.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but I think it's premature to\Nlink that with a mass uprising.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.27,0:02:49.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We are able to stop the influx of\Nrefugees into Nagasaki at the waterfront.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.67,0:02:52.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems you are ignoring certain realities.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.67,0:02:55.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This month, the Coast Guard
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.27,0:03:00.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,has prevented two large ships and sixteen\Nsmaller boats from docking in Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.77,0:03:04.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's obvious that there is an\Ninflux of refugees into Nagasaki.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.47,0:03:05.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.87,0:03:10.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, we have many matters\Nthat require our attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.77,0:03:12.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The particularists?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.67,0:03:15.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then I'd like to know what\NPublic Safety has been doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.97,0:03:20.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,since they bear the responsibility for letting the\Nparticularists who triggered this event run amok.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.97,0:03:24.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Regarding the mass suicide\Nof the Individual Eleven,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.47,0:03:28.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it's unreasonable to have demanded that Public\NSafety be aware of all their locations at all times.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.97,0:03:33.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,After all, even though the\Nparticularists praise the actions
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.67,0:03:37.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,of the Individual Eleven, they maintain\Nthat the Eleven were a league of their own.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.77,0:03:44.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In any case, I think that the Ministry of Defence is\Nthe one responsible for the current refugee situation
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.77,0:03:46.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,After all, their desire to\Nfurther armament procurement
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.87,0:03:49.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,led them to conduct a live-ammunition\Nexercise right in front of the refugees,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.77,0:03:52.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,which stirred them to action.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.27,0:03:55.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If you want to start a chicken-or-egg\Nargument, we'll accept the challenge anytime,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.07,0:04:01.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but isn't it {\i1}your{\i} security department that's\Nwrangling over jurisdiction, even now?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.07,0:04:03.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, if you're going take that position,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.27,0:04:05.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,why is the Maritime Self-Defence\NForce turning a blind eye?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.17,0:04:08.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Before you bring out the jurisdiction issues,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.17,0:04:09.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'd like them to be just a bit more cooperative,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.77,0:04:11.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,considering we're the ones\Nputting our lives on the line!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.87,0:04:13.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,At this point in time,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.47,0:04:17.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,my understanding is that {\i1}we{\i} have been\Ngranted jurisdiction in this refugee matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.07,0:04:19.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Listen to yourself!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.27,0:04:22.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Remember the security-treaty struggle\Nof the previous century?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.67,0:04:25.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Unfortunately for the pro-MoD Diet\Nmembers who came late to the table,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.67,0:04:29.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the police will see to upholding\Nsecurity this time around as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.77,0:04:33.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Such debates are important, but right now,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.57,0:04:36.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,reaching a consensus among\Nthe major agencies is crucial.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.87,0:04:38.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let us break for a moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.78,0:04:58.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems you do not even have\Nthe time to bolster your spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.98,0:05:01.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's partly due to my lack of skill,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.28,0:05:04.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but if everyone remains fixated on their own\Ninterests, they'll lose sight of the real issue...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.58,0:05:10.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,even though now is the time they must cooperate\Nwith each other to deal with the refugee problem...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.98,0:05:12.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Prime Minister,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.38,0:05:18.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,do you know the biggest reason why a nation's\Nmilitary and intelligence agencies deteriorate?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.98,0:05:22.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It is exactly as you just said.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.28,0:05:24.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Gradual death begins
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.58,0:05:29.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,when the leaders of an organisation\Nstarts to use his organisation
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.18,0:05:30.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,as an instrument for furthering his own interests.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.78,0:05:37.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I do feel sorry for making the\NCoast Guard do the dirty work...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.98,0:05:42.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, we cannot be certain that we won't\Nbe blessed with that misfortune ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.08,0:05:43.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's true enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.31,0:05:46.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,By the way,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.81,0:05:51.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,have you obtained any specific information\Nregarding the refugee's actions?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.71,0:05:52.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.81,0:05:55.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Have you heard of "hub cyberbrains"?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.11,0:05:58.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.51,0:06:00.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, please explain.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.59,0:06:06.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Prime Minister, may I link directly with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.79,0:06:07.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.53,0:06:22.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Originally, the concept of a hub,\Nor centre, did not exist in the network.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.03,0:06:26.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, a phenomenon was recently observed
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.43,0:06:28.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,where a host establishes a\Ntype of collaborative entity
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.93,0:06:31.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,by defining a direction for\Nisolated entities on the network
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.43,0:06:35.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and inviting them into his cyberbrain.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.83,0:06:40.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Until now, this was only\Nobserved at a small scale:
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.63,0:06:43.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,communes that formed around small religious\Norganisations and charismatic artists.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.63,0:06:46.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Now, however,\Nsomeone among the refugees has emerged
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.53,0:06:49.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,who is able to placate them and\Npersuade them to stay in this fashion.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.33,0:06:53.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We believe this is the reason behind\Nthe influx of refugees to Nagasaki.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.46,0:06:57.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is this the work of one person...\Nperhaps, the leader?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.46,0:07:00.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Logically speaking, it would be difficult\Nto imagine that it is just one person.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.76,0:07:02.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We cannot be sure,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.56,0:07:04.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but it seems impossible that any single cyberbrain
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.96,0:07:08.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,has the ability to let the consciousness of\Nthree million people harmonise simultaneously.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.76,0:07:11.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, if we were to construe\Nthis construct as a leader,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.66,0:07:13.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,then yes, we could say that\Nhe is something like one.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.36,0:07:15.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.74,0:07:24.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The emergence of such a person would\Nbe a grave threat to the government.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.04,0:07:26.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Please remain on alert.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.24,0:07:28.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.84,0:07:32.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I was hoping to suppress refugee interests
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.64,0:07:34.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and resolve issues from the taxation system side
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.44,0:07:37.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,by repealing the Refugee Special Treatment Act.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.24,0:07:41.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It must mean that there was a political\Nenemy who used that to his advantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.84,0:07:43.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Do not let it affect you too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.64,0:07:47.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Actually...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.84,0:07:50.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have one more thing I'd like you to investigate.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.54,0:07:52.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.34,0:07:55.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In regard to the security pact,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.24,0:07:57.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it seems there are some pro-MoD Diet members
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.14,0:08:00.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,who are in collusion with\Nthe former Dai-Nippon Giken.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.44,0:08:04.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I believe that the significance\Nof this security pact
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.54,0:08:08.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,lies in the fact that our country, as the only nation\Nin the world to possess radiation removal technology,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.24,0:08:11.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,may gain equal, if not superior,\Nfooting with the American Empire.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.64,0:08:15.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The AE has been dependent on nuclear deterrence.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.24,0:08:17.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If that is no longer viable,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.94,0:08:21.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I am willing to postpone the security pact.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.74,0:08:24.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, some of the Diet\Nmembers and captains of industry
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.74,0:08:26.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,do not care about such principles.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.14,0:08:28.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If this continues,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.64,0:08:31.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,our nation will never become independent!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.44,0:08:34.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Where did you obtain that information?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.74,0:08:36.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,From a source in the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.84,0:08:40.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then we will investigate the cash flow right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.04,0:08:41.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Just one thing...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.04,0:08:46.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are you issuing this order for\Nyour own personal interests,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.34,0:08:49.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,or to preserve a political ideology?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.14,0:08:52.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There is no need for an answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.34,0:08:55.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.88,0:09:14.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I should've realised this sooner.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.48,0:09:19.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Prime Minister Kayabuki is exactly\Nthe type of person you like, Chief.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.38,0:09:21.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What, you only realised this now?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.78,0:09:25.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I can't beat you, Chief.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.67,0:09:33.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,By pro-MoD Diet members... she was talking about\NChief Cabinet Secretary Takakura, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.57,0:09:34.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Probably.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.17,0:09:40.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'd find it difficult to believe\Nhe's doing this just for money.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.07,0:09:44.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Takakura is pro-America and pro-right-wing, no?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.57,0:09:45.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.97,0:09:50.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He is an old-timer in the military industrial complex who\Nhas yet to discard blind trust in the American Empire.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.37,0:09:52.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,From his point of view,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.77,0:09:58.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,we can increase the value of the radiation removal\Ntechnology, which lost value after the war ended,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.17,0:10:04.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,by joining forces with the American Empire and using\Nit as a new deterrent force against other nations.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.47,0:10:08.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,By doing that, he can secure bribes\Nand also save face for the right wing
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.07,0:10:11.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,without having to pursue\Nfurther armament expansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.97,0:10:14.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's very different from the\Nindependence-cooperation route
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.57,0:10:17.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,that Prime Minister Kayabuki is arguing for.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.37,0:10:21.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He's the top guy in the Cabinet\NIntelligence Agency as well, isn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.67,0:10:24.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Besides, Gouda has a history of having overseen
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.47,0:10:27.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the production of the Japanese Miracle at\Nthe former Dai-Nippon Giken.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.47,0:10:33.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Inducing terrorism by refugees,\Nthe AE-Japan security pact, and nuclear power...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.76,0:10:39.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Looks like her revenge...\Nis worthy of our assistance.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.43,0:11:01.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're tired of waiting for\Nyou, Prime Minister Kayabuki.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.93,0:11:06.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I will be there immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.49,0:11:20.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Senpai!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.39,0:11:22.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's up, Azuma?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.99,0:11:25.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We haven't been summoned...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.89,0:11:27.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,is it really okay for us not to join in?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.09,0:11:30.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What about the investigation\Non the Individual Eleven?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.79,0:11:33.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They are less active than the refugees,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.49,0:11:36.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,so we kind of thought they\Nwere, you know, boring...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.89,0:11:37.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You idiots!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.29,0:11:39.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What do you mean, "boring"?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.79,0:11:40.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's your job!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.29,0:11:43.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Jeez, you guys have a long way to go!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.54,0:11:51.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Back then, the pointless war over Eurasian\Nhegemony had only just ended, after all...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.04,0:11:54.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I snuck into the Peninsula\Na couple of times back then,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.84,0:11:57.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but it was already pretty modernised.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.64,0:11:58.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Did you guys start already?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.04,0:12:00.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Not yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.24,0:12:02.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I was doing warm-up exercises\Nwhile waiting for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.64,0:12:05.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let's get started.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.64,0:12:10.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,My sympathies for having to work\Novertime so soon after coming back.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.14,0:12:11.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.94,0:12:12.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.64,0:12:31.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In the year 2024, when nations were\Nexhausted from the fourth world war,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.14,0:12:34.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the American Empire called for the deployment
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.24,0:12:38.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,of UN troops to the Peninsula,\Nwhere internal conflict still continued.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.14,0:12:41.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That action triggered our SDF deployment, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.24,0:12:47.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Actually, the American Empire started its\Nresurrection as the world's dominant power
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.94,0:12:50.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,by using the deployment as a\Nway to obtain excavation rights
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.94,0:12:54.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to the uranium mines in the Northern\NPeninsula from the unified government, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.14,0:12:56.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There's that side to it, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.54,0:13:00.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But despite the fact that the\NEmpire's intentions were transparent,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.14,0:13:04.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Japan couldn't have possibly refused the UN, considering\Nhow enthused it was about wartime military procurement.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.24,0:13:09.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Thus, this became the first trial for the SDF,\Nwhich had been able to avoid actual combat
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.24,0:13:11.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,throughout two world wars,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.94,0:13:14.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,aside from the recapture of Nemuro.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.14,0:13:18.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But people like you and the Major
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.24,0:13:21.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,were overseas unofficially during the\Nwar, weren't they?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.44,0:13:22.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.04,0:13:25.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's too bad that the Prime Minister at\Nthe time was killed by a terrorist bomb,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.04,0:13:29.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,since he was one of the few politicians\Nwho had an international perspective.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.04,0:13:32.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Because of these behind the scenes issues,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.14,0:13:36.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the government had strict control of the\Nmedia in order to suppress domestic opinion
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.94,0:13:42.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and decided to deploy the PKF to Shinuiju\NState, which was thought to be relatively safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.54,0:13:45.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I can still remember the uproar then,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.64,0:13:50.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but I guess I gradually grew disinterested\Nas the news kept showing the SDF,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.74,0:13:53.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,spending time with the residents,\Nand looking out of place.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.64,0:13:54.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Not surprising.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.14,0:13:57.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The reality of it was rather\Ndifferent, actually...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.34,0:14:00.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The agency that worked behind\Nthe scenes to control the media
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.84,0:14:04.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,was the current Cabinet\NIntelligence Agency's predecessor,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.44,0:14:06.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the Cabinet Press Agency,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.74,0:14:09.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So, what was the reality for the PKF?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.04,0:14:10.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh, yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.04,0:14:14.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems it was much worse than we'd thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.04,0:14:22.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Kuze was stationed with the\Nlast mobile company to arrive.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.64,0:14:27.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,At the time, Shinuiju was a Special\NAdministrative Region and a trade centre,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.54,0:14:30.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,making it exempt from attacks.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.24,0:14:31.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But after the unified government was established,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.84,0:14:35.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the remnants of the defeated People's\NArmy chose as their battlefield
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.04,0:14:39.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,a rural area about twenty\Nkilometres east of Shinuiju.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.74,0:14:42.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,After you cross the border,\NI guess it's all mountains.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.74,0:14:45.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,More like a mountain pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.74,0:14:47.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The altitude was 800 metres, at most.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.84,0:14:52.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So, it was ideal for guerilla warfare.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.94,0:14:56.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Soon after the cyborg infantry\Narrived, it was decided that two
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.24,0:14:59.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,units would be deployed as a\Ncounter-guerilla punitive force,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.44,0:15:02.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,so they began moving into the frigid mountains.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.94,0:15:06.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This was the first time units were equipped\Nwith hybrid cyborgs on the battlefield,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.34,0:15:09.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but the PKF-spec hybrid cyborgs would\Nnot have experienced much discomfort,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.14,0:15:14.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,even while advancing through\Nsnow in -20°C weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.04,0:15:17.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,At the time,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.34,0:15:19.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the main infantry was on\Nheightened alert after receiving an
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.99,0:15:22.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,intelligence report that the last\Nelite troops of the People's Army
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.94,0:15:24.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,were plotting to attack Shinuiju State.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.84,0:15:31.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Kuze's company was to circle north,\Naround the enemy, and launch a preemptive strike.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.74,0:15:35.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, on the way,\NKuze's platoon found a refugee camp
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.24,0:15:40.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,along a river on the border that was not\Nmentioned in the intelligence report.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.74,0:15:47.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The camp was being looted by soldiers\Nof the People's Army who had,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.54,0:15:51.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,for all intents and purposes, become bandits.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.72,0:15:57.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Seeing this happen before their eyes,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.02,0:16:00.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the platoon was spurred into\Ncombat by moral indignation.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.62,0:16:04.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,While there were only thirty of them\Nagainst one hundred and twenty soldiers,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.72,0:16:10.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the fighting quickly reached a conclusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.62,0:16:14.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Kuze's platoon was a group\Nof elites with cyborg bodies,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.42,0:16:20.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,while those who were attacking the\Ncamp were mostly unarmed and starved,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.12,0:16:22.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,even if they were former soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.76,0:16:37.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,After that, the PKF received several\Nreports on the People's Army,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.16,0:16:39.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but that was their only actual combat.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.76,0:16:43.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They were forced to stay on\Nalert due to the extreme cold
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.06,0:16:45.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and the possibility of a\Nguerilla attack at any time,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.06,0:16:48.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but for the main infantry\Npositioned back in the city,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.46,0:16:51.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the tension was not that great.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.46,0:16:53.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's the footage I remember seeing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.26,0:16:54.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.76,0:16:59.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But after a while, a problem surfaced\Nin the platoon camp out in the farmland:
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.66,0:17:00.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,PTSD, huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.06,0:17:02.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.56,0:17:05.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.36,0:17:10.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The experience of having massacred people in their first\Nfight, not to mention the fact that it was very uneven,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.26,0:17:13.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,began to eat away at the young soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.36,0:17:16.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Those who still had their\Noriginal lungs and other organs
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.06,0:17:20.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,tried synthetic alcohol and hashish\Nthat had been brought in by refugees,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.16,0:17:26.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,desperate to escape the nightmarish\Nflashbacks of the massacre.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.24,0:17:33.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,When order gradually began\Nto break down in the SDF,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.14,0:17:37.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the Japanese media pelted them\Nwith insensitive comments.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.24,0:17:47.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The massacre at the refugee camp had\Nnot reached the media due to censorship,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.54,0:17:51.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but their criticism of the men's behaviour\Nwas all the more severe because of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.74,0:17:56.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In addition, their freedom was restricted by\Npolicies designed to prevent the men's disgrace
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.24,0:17:58.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,from reaching the media.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.44,0:18:02.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They were even barred from returning to Japan.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.14,0:18:05.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Sounds almost like an isolation ward...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.24,0:18:06.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, on top of that,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.24,0:18:11.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the refugee camp massacre near the\Nborder was leaked to part of the media
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.64,0:18:16.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and a false rumour that it had been\Nexecuted by the JSDF began to circulate.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.14,0:18:21.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The farmers vehemently condemned the\NJSDF and demanded an explanation.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.14,0:18:26.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, under the media censorship\Nneither the young soldiers
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.84,0:18:30.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,nor even their superior officers\Ncould defend themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.74,0:18:34.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They could only retreat to their tents.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.64,0:18:38.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,One day, after these conditions\Nhad gone on for a while,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.04,0:18:42.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,one of the local journalists apparently\Nmade a comment to one of the soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.24,0:18:44.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He probably thought
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.64,0:18:49.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,he was just making a sarcastic comment to\Na soldier who no longer had his own lungs.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.44,0:18:53.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.94,0:18:55.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You there.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.04,0:18:58.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,do you know the meaning of the word "assassin"?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.74,0:19:03.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's an Arabic word for someone who eats hashish.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.14,0:19:09.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Muslim assassins, who killed the Crusaders\Nthat recaptured Jerusalem in the eleventh century,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.24,0:19:13.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,attacked while in a dream like\Nhaze after smoking hashish.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.42,0:19:19.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Crusaders then called them\N"assassins" and feared them.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.42,0:19:23.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Did you guys see this as paradise\Nbecause of that stuff, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.12,0:19:25.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How long will you consider yourselves as guests
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.02,0:19:28.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,after invading someone else's country,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.42,0:19:30.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,eh, you murderers?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.88,0:19:34.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Wh-What?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.98,0:19:35.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,True...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.48,0:19:39.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,maybe we did think of ourselves as guests.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.52,0:19:51.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Can you give me that... for this?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.12,0:20:01.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Kuze then changed his rifle for the\Ncamera and entered the refugee camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.32,0:20:05.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And, what'd he do?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.02,0:20:07.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.12,0:20:12.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He just carried the camera around and observed\Nthe refugees lives through the finder,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.82,0:20:15.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,as well as making origami figures.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.72,0:20:16.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I don't get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.92,0:20:17.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.02,0:20:20.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have no idea what his real intentions were.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.92,0:20:24.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But a while after he entered the\Ncamp, strange things began to happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.02,0:20:29.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,First, the elderly gradually became interested\Nin Kuze and started offering him drinks.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.32,0:20:33.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Next the children began asking him\Nto fold paper planes, and so on.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.82,0:20:37.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The refugees drew closer and closer to\NKuze, who didn't say a single word.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.12,0:20:44.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,By the next day, women as well as\Nmen would take turns talking to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.12,0:20:49.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Kuze would just happily watch them,\Nand sometimes, take their pictures.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.32,0:20:51.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.12,0:20:52.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And them?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.12,0:20:53.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Kuze continued doing this until three months later
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.72,0:20:58.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,when the People's Army surrendered and\Nthe SDF was cleared of its obligations.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.32,0:21:02.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Everyone in the media stopped talking\Nabout the massacre after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.42,0:21:08.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The day before the SDF was to return to\NJapan, Kuze disappeared from the camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.82,0:21:12.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,A photo was left at the camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.22,0:21:16.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What about his whereabouts after that?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.12,0:21:19.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He supposedly crossed the border and went west,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.02,0:21:21.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but this is not certain either.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.92,0:21:25.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,While I was investigating where\Nhe wandered and what he was doing,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.62,0:21:29.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I interviewed a man who had returned\Nfrom a Taiwanese refugee city.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.82,0:21:33.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He said he saw a man who\Nmight have been Kuze there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.12,0:21:37.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The hair on his cybernetic body\Nhad turned completely white,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.32,0:21:39.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but he was definitely Kuze,\Naccording to the witness.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.42,0:21:43.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,As "proof", there were always\Npeople hanging around that man
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.72,0:21:46.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,who looked like they were enjoying themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.62,0:21:51.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are you of Japanese descent?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.52,0:21:52.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.42,0:21:55.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh. You can speak?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.32,0:22:07.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh, you are back, Major?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.62,0:22:09.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes. I was listening.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.82,0:22:13.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's an interesting story, to be sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.76,0:22:19.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Representative.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.26,0:22:23.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The hub cyberbrain's filtering\Narray proved difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.46,0:22:26.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but we finally managed to reverse-trace\Nthe refugees' cyberbrains.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.96,0:22:28.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,As we'd thought, it seems to be Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.36,0:22:32.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We have requested the NSA to corroborate this,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.76,0:22:35.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,so we should be able to get\Nvisual confirmation soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.64,0:23:10.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Finding out a galaxy
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.54,0:23:14.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,of planets and stars within me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.14,0:23:17.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Listening to each of them
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.34,0:23:21.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,singing the same silent melody.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.24,0:23:25.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I've never seen such beauty
